{
  "tema": 5151,
  "slug": "subjuntivo-presente-er-ir",
  "titulo": "Conjugate regular -er and -ir verbs in the present subjunctive",
  "subtitulo": "-er and -ir verbs switch to a: coma, vivas, abramos.",
  "foto": "t02.jpg",
  "regla": "Take the present-tense yo form, drop the -o and add -a, -as, -a, -amos, -an. -er and -ir verbs switch to a.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Regular **-er** and **-ir** verbs follow **the same pattern** in the present subjunctive, and the pattern includes a change of vowel at the end. The stem is the **yo** form of the present (**yo bebo** → **beb-**), and the **-o** is replaced with:"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "present **yo** form",
            "minus **-o**",
            "**-a, -as, -a, -amos, -an**"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Person",
            "Ending",
            "comer",
            "vivir"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "yo",
              "-a",
              "coma",
              "viva"
            ],
            [
              "tú",
              "-as",
              "comas",
              "vivas"
            ],
            [
              "él, ella, usted",
              "-a",
              "coma",
              "viva"
            ],
            [
              "nosotros",
              "-amos",
              "comamos",
              "vivamos"
            ],
            [
              "ustedes, ellos",
              "-an",
              "coman",
              "vivan"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**-er and -ir verbs switch to the vowel a**, while **-ar** verbs switch to **e** ([[5063|-ar in the subjunctive]]). In the subjunctive, **-er** and **-ir** have no difference at all."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: they cross over. The **a** verbs go to **e**, and the **e** and **i** verbs go to **a**. Like in jiu-jitsu, always to the other side."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Es mejor que ==coma== despacio antes de entrenar.",
              "en": "It's better if I eat slowly before training."
            },
            {
              "es": "No quiero que ==bebas== cerveza en la playa.",
              "en": "I don't want you to drink beer on the beach."
            },
            {
              "es": "Espero que ==vivas== feliz en tu depa nuevo.",
              "en": "I hope you live happily in your new apartment."
            },
            {
              "es": "Quizás ==abran== el regalo más tarde.",
              "en": "They may open the present later."
            },
            {
              "es": "Espero que ==reciban== muchos regalos.",
              "en": "I hope you all get lots of presents."
            },
            {
              "es": "¡No ==leamos== hoy! Vámonos a surfear.",
              "en": "Let's not read today! Let's go surf."
            },
            {
              "es": "No ==escriban== en esa hoja, por favor.",
              "en": "Don't write on that sheet, please. (to several people)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trampa",
      "titulo": "The trap",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "The **-er** / **-ir** subjunctive ends in **a**, which looks like the ordinary present of an **-ar** verb. Don't go on habit: after the trigger, the **a** is the right one."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "pares",
          "lista": [
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Espero que vives feliz."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Espero que vivas feliz."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "After **espero que**, use the **a**."
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "No quiero que comes tanto."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "No quiero que comas tanto."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Es mejor que Beto aprende rápido."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Es mejor que Beto aprenda rápido."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "**Es mejor que** also takes the subjunctive."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "usos",
      "titulo": "The same form, other jobs",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "usos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "forma": "Quiero que comas.",
              "texto": "After a trigger with **que**.",
              "aqui": true
            },
            {
              "forma": "No comas eso.",
              "texto": "The negative **tú** command. See [[9255|negative commands]]."
            },
            {
